 '即使partial执行，DeepSeek-R1-14B的异常方差结构（residual=42%）进一步瓦解了 universal item\n    dominance叙事。但hardware confound无法排除（单GPU结果）， 且sample size=2个14B模型太少做scale-effect的causal\n    claim。reframe中作为 supplementary evidence用，不作为独立contribution。\n\n    '\n- name: Fine-tuning G-study (RoBERTa)\n  plan_id: exp-006\n  description: 'RoBERTa-large on SST-2/MNLI/RTE/COPA。6 seeds × 3 learning rates ×\n    4 data shuffles × 3 GPUs × 2 precisions = 432 runs/task × 4 tasks = 1,728 runs。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    item_variance_share_sst2: 0.15\n    item_variance_share_mnli: 0.12\n    item_variance_share_rte: 0.2\n    item_variance_share_copa: 0.08\n    learning_rate_main_effect_avg: 0.18\n    seed_main_effect_avg: 0.08\n    data_shuffle_main_effect_avg: 0.06\n    precision_main_effect_avg: 0.02\n    lr_seed_interaction_avg: 0.1\n    residual_avg: 0.22\n    g_coefficient_sst2: 0.55\n    g_coefficient_rte: 0.48\n    g_coefficient_copa: 0.35\n    training_vs_inference_variance_correlation: 0.15\n  result_rationale: 'Fine-tuning的方差结构与inference fundamentally不同。Learning rate是最大的\n    可归因方差来源（~18%），因为它直接控制模型converge到loss landscape的哪个 basin，不同basin对不同items的predictions质性不同。seed:lr交互高达10%因为\n    不同seed的weight initialization在不同lr下converge到不同local minima。 item_id在fine-tuning中方差占比更低（8-20%），因为fine-tuning本身改变了\n    model-item的关系——同一个item在不同training run中的难度会变（unlike inference where model weights\n    are fixed）。COPA尤其低（8%）因为dataset 只有400 items，且causal reasoning tasks的learning dynamics更chaotic。\n    residual=22%反映了training过程中unmodeled的随机性（CUDA非确定性在训练中 比推理中更显著，因为每个gradient step都累积噪声）。与inference方差结构\n    的correlation极低（r=0.15），说明inference-based的D-study budget不能 指导training-time的reproducibility。这个发现独立于inference\n    story，可以 作为separate contribution线——即使inference的item dominance不成立， fine-tuning的方差归因本身也是novel的。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 8: Fine-tuning Variance Decomposition by Task'\n    columns:\n    - Component\n    - SST-2\n    - MNLI\n    - RTE\n    - COPA\n    - Average\n    rows:\n    - - learning_rate\n      - 16.0%\n      - 20.0%\n      - 18.0%\n      - 17.0%\n      - 17.8%\n    - - residual\n      - 20.0%\n      - 22.0%\n      - 21.0%\n      - 25.0%\n      - 22.0%\n    - - item_id\n      - 15.0%\n      - 12.0%\n      - 20.0%\n      - 8.0%\n      - 13.8%\n    - - lr:seed\n      - 10.0%\n      - 11.0%\n      - 9.0%\n      - 10.0%\n      - 10.0%\n    - - seed\n      - 8.0%\n      - 7.0%\n      - 9.0%\n      - 8.0%\n      - 8.0%\n    - - data_shuffle\n      - 7.0%\n      - 6.0%\n      - 5.0%\n      - 6.0%\n      - 6.0%\n    - - seed:item\n      - 5.0%\n      - 4.0%\n      - 4.0%\n      - 6.0%\n      - 4.8%\n    - - precision\n      - 2.0%\n      - 2.5%\n      - 1.8%\n      - 2.2%\n      - 2.1%\n    - - lr:item\n      - 8.0%\n      - 7.0%\n      - 6.0%\n      - 9.0%\n      - 7.5%\n    - - all other\n      - 9.0%\n      - 8.5%\n      - 6.2%\n      - 8.8%\n      - 8.1%\n  - name: 'Table 9: Inference vs Fine-tuning Variance Hierarchy'\n    columns:\n    - Rank\n    - Inference (MMLU)\n    - Fine-tuning (avg)\n    rows:\n    - - 1st\n      - residual (28%)\n      - residual (22%)\n    - - 2nd\n      - item_id (24%)\n      - learning_rate (18%)\n    - - 3rd\n      - temp:item (5.5%)\n      - item_id (14%)\n    - - 4th\n      - prompt:item (4.8%)\n      - lr:seed (10%)\n    - - 5th\n      - precision:item (3.5%)\n      - seed (8%)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Side-by-side stacked bars: inference (exp-001 MMLU) vs fine-tuning (exp-006 average)的方差分解，颜色编码相同components以突出hierarchy的质性差异。'\n  - 'Scatter plot: 每个component在inference vs fine-tuning中的variance share，理想情况下应在diagonal上。worst档下points远离diagonal，r=0.15的correlation在plot上视觉明显。'\n  analysis: 'exp-006在worst档下是最有价值的hedge。即使inference story崩溃，fine-tuning的 方差归因是genuinely\n    novel的——此前没有研究用G-theory分解fine-tuning的完整 facet structure。learning rate dominance（18%）、lr:seed交互（10%）、以及\n    inference-training方差结构的decorrelation（r=0.15）都是publishable findings。 这条线可以独立于inference\n    story发展，在worst档下成为paper的saving grace。 potential title angle: \"What makes fine-tuning\n    unreproducible? A G-theory decomposition reveals learning rate × seed interactions\n    dominate.\"\n\n    '\n- name: LayerCast precision mitigation\n  plan_id: exp-007\n  description: 'LayerCast（FP16 storage + FP32 compute）作为额外precision条件测试方差减少量。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    layercast_accuracy: 0.672\n    layercast_vs_bf16_accuracy_delta: 0.001\n    variance_reduction_vs_fp16: 0.003\n    precision_component_with_layercast: 0.012\n    precision_item_interaction_with_layercast: 0.03\n    practical_significance: negligible\n  result_rationale: '在worst档下，exp-001已经显示precision main effect仅1.5%（confound修复后）。\n    LayerCast的FP16 storage + FP32 compute在理论上应该给出接近FP32的结果，但 由于FP32本身与BF16/FP16的差异已经很小（Δaccuracy=0.002），LayerCast的\n    额外收益几乎为零。precision:item交互从3.5%微降到3.0%，不具有实际意义。 这个结果说明precision本来就不是主要方差来源（confound修复后），mitigation\n    策略针对的是一个已经很小的问题。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 10: Precision Conditions Including LayerCast'\n    columns:\n    - Condition\n    - Accuracy\n    - Precision Variance Share\n    - Precision:Item Share\n    rows:\n    - - FP32\n      - '0.670'\n      - 1.5%\n      - 3.5%\n    - - BF16\n      - '0.672'\n      - —\n      - —\n    - - FP16\n      - '0.671'\n      - —\n      - —\n    - - LayerCast (FP16+FP32)\n      - '0.672'\n      - 1.2%\n      - 3.0%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart with error bars: 4种precision条件的accuracy分布，展示LayerCast与BF16几乎重叠，视觉上传达''precision\n    mitigation对一个已经很小的问题没有意义''。'\n  analysis: 'exp-007在worst档下基本是negative/null result。可以用一句话mention作为 supplementary\n    finding（\"LayerCast provides negligible additional benefit when the float32 engine\n    confound is properly controlled\"），但不值得 dedicated space。主要价值是排除了precision作为重要方差来源的可能性。\n\n    '\n- name: MATH benchmark extension\n  plan_id: exp-008\n  description: 'MATH benchmark 200 items，测试reasoning-heavy tasks中CoT引入的额外方差。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    item_variance_share_math: 0.1\n    residual_share_math: 0.4\n    seed_main_effect_math: 0.07\n    seed_item_interaction_math: 0.12\n    temperature_main_effect_math: 0.1\n    temperature_item_interaction_math: 0.15\n    prompt_item_interaction_math: 0.03\n    g_coefficient_math: 0.3\n    cot_length_variance_correlation: 0.65\n    items_needed_g90_math: 2200\n  result_rationale: 'MATH是最extreme的reasoning benchmark，CoT生成过程中的每个token都是一个 采样点，长推理链（avg\n    200+ tokens）意味着seed和temperature的随机性被200+ 次multiplicative放大。因此seed:item（12%）和temperature:item（15%）极高，\n    temperature main effect达10%（在其他benchmark上<2%），因为temperature 直接控制采样diversity，在长chain中的累积效应是非线性的。item_id仅10%——\n    比GSM8K更低——因为MATH problems的难度更多由解题路径的存在性决定，而非 item本身的知识内容，solution path的发现受seed/temperature强烈影响。\n    residual高达40%是worst档中最高的，反映了MATH推理过程中大量不可归因的 随机性（错误的推理链、self-correction失败、格式解析错误等）。G=0.30是\n    所有benchmark中最低的，G≥0.90需要2200 items，完全不切实际（MATH全集仅 5000题）。这个结果是\"no universal recipe\"论点的最强证据——如果连G≥0.90\n    的item threshold在不同benchmark间差3-4倍，prescriptive budget毫无意义。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 11: MATH Variance Decomposition vs Other Benchmarks'\n    columns:\n    - Component\n    - MMLU\n    - GSM8K\n    - MATH\n    rows:\n    - - residual\n      - 28%\n      - 35%\n      - 40%\n    - - item_id\n      - 24%\n      - 12%\n      - 10%\n    - - temp:item\n      - 5.5%\n      - 18%\n      - 15%\n    - - seed:item\n      - 1.8%\n      - 14%\n      - 12%\n    - - temperature\n      - 1.2%\n      - 8%\n      - 10%\n    - - seed\n      - 0.3%\n      - 5%\n      - 7%\n    - - G coefficient\n      - '0.42'\n      - '0.38'\n      - '0.30'\n    - - Items for G≥0.90\n      - '850'\n      - '1400'\n      - '2200'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter plot: CoT生成长度(tokens) vs item-level accuracy variance，展示正相关（r=0.65）——推理链越长，evaluation\n    variance越大。这是mechanistic explanation。'\n  - 'Gradient spectrum bar: 从MMLU→ARC→HellaSwag→GSM8K→MATH的G coefficient递减趋势，visual\n    argument for benchmark-conditional variance。'\n  analysis: MATH是worst档叙事的exclamation mark。G=0.30意味着当前practice下MATH evaluation基本是noise-dominated的。结合exp-002的GSM8K结果，形成清晰的\n    gradient：knowledge-retrieval tasks（MMLU）→ moderate reasoning（ARC）→ generation-heavy\n    reasoning（GSM8K/MATH）的方差结构systematically shifts from item-conditional to seed/temperature-conditional。这个gradient本身\n    是一个contribution——它解释了为什么reasoning benchmark的reproduction rates historically更低，并提供了mechanistic\n    account（CoT length amplifies sampling noise）。\n","numLines":716,"startLine":1,"totalLines":716}}}
